// What a fight pays and what things cost, tuned while the game runs.
//
// The game reads this file again whenever it is saved (BIMS_REWARDS names
// another). The next enemy down and the next price asked take the new
// numbers. A field left out is the built-in value, and a file that does not
// parse keeps the last good numbers (the reason is printed on the terminal).
//
//   site_xp                 what a site is worth in experience on the run's
//                           first day, to every player: each enemy down pays
//                           its wave's share of it, once, to every classed
//                           crew member within fifty tiles (an elite's site
//                           twice that; the bonus wave half again)
//   site_xp_growth_percent  how much more a site is worth every day after,
//                           in per cent, compounded
//   site_money              what a site pays in euros on the run's first
//                           day, a player's worth for every player into the
//                           pool: each enemy down pays its wave's share of
//                           it, once (a Husk or a pistol a tenth less, a
//                           Warden or a Guardian a tenth more; an elite's
//                           site half again; the bonus wave a quarter again)
//   site_money_growth_percent  how much more a site pays every day after,
//                           in per cent, compounded
//   defense_bounty_percent  how much of that a defence pays (100 = the same
//                           as an attack, 0 = nothing)
//   bot_bounty_percent      how much of that is paid when one of the crew's
//                           bots took the enemy down, in per cent
//   player_bounty_percent   how much when a player took it down (a
//                           commander's reinforcements and his medic count
//                           as his own), in per cent
//   bounty_waits_for_clear  true: the money waits until the site is cleared
//                           and is lost if the crew leave first;
//                           false: paid the moment the enemy goes down
//   buyback                 what bringing a dead player's Bim back costs
//   shelf_price_percent     a trader's shelf prices, in per cent
//
// The values below are the built-in ones.
(
    site_xp: 60,
    site_xp_growth_percent: 12,
    site_money: 850,
    site_money_growth_percent: 17,
    defense_bounty_percent: 100,
    bot_bounty_percent: 100,
    player_bounty_percent: 110,
    bounty_waits_for_clear: true,
    buyback: 5000,
    shelf_price_percent: 100,
)
